export default "# Case Study: Document Editor Workflow\n\n> **Status:** Architecture Blueprint  \n> **Date:** 2026-07-17  \n> **Tags:** A2UI, Lexical Editor, Agentic Flow, Three-Column Panel System\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Prompt Composer Console uses its three-column panel system to transform the chat prompt from a question-answer interface into a **document editing workspace**. The AI agent becomes a document organizer. The left prompt panel collapses when no longer needed. The third column becomes the primary workspace.\n\n---\n\n## Flow\n\n### Phase 1 — Discovery (Console)\n1. User opens the Console and clicks the **Docs** filter in the toolbar\n2. A card appears: *\"Storybook Documentation Editor\"* — this is an AI agent prompt packaged as a card\n3. The card's description explains: *\"Organize and edit your project's markdown documentation\"*\n\n### Phase 2 — Agent Assembly (Composer)\n4. User clicks the card → the prompt loads into the **left column** (Composer)\n5. The AI agent has pre-built a prompt with:\n   - **System Role:** *\"You are a documentation editor. Present all markdown files as a dropdown selector. When the user selects one, load it into the editor and collapse the left panel.\"*\n   - **Tools dropdown:** populated with all 17 Storybook markdown files\n   - **Constraints:** *\"Only show markdown files from the project. Allow the user to select one, then collapse.\"*\n\n### Phase 3 — Selection & Execution\n6. User selects a markdown from the Tools dropdown (e.g., *\"Architecture Vision\"*)\n7. User clicks **Run**\n8. The AI emits: `<load_tool name=\"lexical-editor\" doc=\"docs/Architecture_Vision.mdx\"/>`\n9. The third column loads the markdown content into the Lexical Editor\n10. The **left column collapses** — the prompt has served its purpose\n\n### Phase 4 — Editing (Workspace)\n11. User is now in a two-panel layout:\n    - **Third column (center):** Lexical Editor with the markdown document\n    - **Right column:** AI chat assistant (*\"Hello Clippy\"*)\n12. User edits the document with full rich-text controls\n13. The AI assistant in the chat can:\n    - Check writing quality: `<check_writing/>`\n    - Apply suggestions: `<apply_suggestion id=\"...\"/>`\n    - Format text: `<format_text type=\"bold\"/>`\n    - Insert tables, links, code blocks\n14. Saved versions auto-commit to Milvus for rollback\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     CONSOLE TOOLBAR                         │\n│  [Popular] [Templates] [Groups] [Docs] ← filter            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐   │\n│  │ Doc Card │  │ Doc Card │  │ Doc Card │  │ Doc Card │   │\n│  │ .mdx     │  │ .mdx     │  │ .md       │  │ .mdx     │   │\n│  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  LEFT COLUMN          │  THIRD COLUMN     │  RIGHT COLUMN  │\n│  (collapsed)          │  Lexical Editor   │  AI Chat       │\n│                       │                   │                │\n│                       │  # Architecture   │  \"Would you    │\n│                       │  ## Overview      │   like me to   │\n│                       │  The Prompt       │   check the    │\n│                       │  Composer...      │   writing?\"    │\n│                       │                   │                │\n│                       │  [B] [I] [U] ... │  [Send]        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why This Works\n\n### Panel Flexibility\nThe three-column system isn't rigid. Panels collapse when their job is done. The left column holds the prompt only during assembly. Once executed, it disappears — leaving the document as the focus.\n\n### AI as Organizer, Not Just Responder\nThe AI doesn't just answer questions. It **organizes content** — building dropdowns, filtering options, preparing the workspace. It's a project assistant, not a chatbot.\n\n### Document-Centric Editing\nOnce the document loads, the user isn't prompting anymore. They're editing. The chat becomes a sidekick: check writing, format text, insert elements. The prompt phase is complete.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Status\n\n| Component | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Docs filter in toolbar | ✅ Built |\n| StorybookDocCard component | ✅ Built |\n| StorybookDocRegistry (17 docs) | ✅ Built |\n| StorybookDocLoader (Vite glob) | ✅ Built |\n| Click → load in Lexical Editor | 🔧 Wiring in progress |\n| Left column collapse on doc open | ⬜ Pending |\n| AI-generated dropdown in prompt | ⬜ Pending |\n| AI chat as document assistant | ⬜ Pending |\n\n---\n\n## Future: AI-Generated Cards\n\nThe Docs filter is the first example. The architecture supports any AI-generated content appearing as cards:\n\n- **Project files** — AI scans the repo and presents files as cards\n- **Meeting notes** — AI generates summary cards from transcripts\n- **Code reviews** — AI packages review comments as editable cards\n- **Design specs** — Figma-linked components as interactive cards\n\nEach follows the same pattern: card → prompt assembly → execution → document editing.\n"